{"step_index":168,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:55:23Z","content":"### 🚀 Update Completed & Fully Operational\n\nThe **Brew & Bloom Café** platform has been enhanced with all requested features and refined with zero breaking changes:\n\n---\n\n### 🔑 Key Enhancements Added in this Step\n\n1. **Interactive UPI Payment Workflow**:\n   * When **Instant UPI Payment** is selected at checkout, a dynamic container appears featuring:\n     * Deep-link button: `upi://pay?pa=yourname@upi&pn=Brew%20Bloom%20Cafe&am=...&cu=INR` (launches Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, or BHIM on mobile devices).\n     * Live QR Code: Dynamically generated for scanning from any mobile banking/UPI app.\n     * Clear demo mode disclosure: Explains that payments are simulated without charging bank accounts unless connected to a live merchant gateway.\n     * Cash on Delivery remains available for instant placement.\n\n2. **Instant Demo Seed Order**:\n   * An initial active order (`#BNB789DEMO` for *Ananya Mukherjee*) is automatically seeded in demo mode.\n   * Visiting **[`order-tracking.html`](http://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html)**, **[`admin.html`](http://localhost:3000/admin.html)**, or **[`driver.html`](http://localhost:3000/driver.html)** immediately renders live delivery data, a route on the map, and interactive controls without requiring an order to be placed first.\n\n3. **Kitchen Audio Chimes**:\n   * Uses the native Web Audio API (offline, zero external audio dependencies) to play a chime when the kitchen board refreshes or updates an order status in [`admin.html`](http://localhost:3000/admin.html).\n\n4. **All 10 Endpoints Tested & Verified**:\n   * Storefront (`/`), Live Tracking (`/order-tracking.html`), Kitchen Admin (`/admin.html`), Driver Dispatch (`/driver.html`), CSS, and all JavaScript modules return `HTTP 200 OK`.\n   * Node.js ES Module syntax checks passed with zero errors.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Quick Access Links\n\n| Page | URL | Credentials / Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Storefront & Menu** | [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) | Full menu, cart drawer & checkout |\n| **Customer Tracking** | [http://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html](http://localhost:3000/order-tracking.html) | Live map, 6-stage tracker & scooter simulation |\n| **Kitchen Admin** | [http://localhost:3000/admin.html](http://localhost:3000/admin.html) | PIN: **`brew2026`** |\n| **Driver Fleet App** | [http://localhost:3000/driver.html](http://localhost:3000/driver.html) | PIN: **`driver2026`** |\n\n*All deployment instructions, database schemas, and configuration guides are saved in the project artifact: [`brew-and-bloom-guide.md`](file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b76faff2-d711-4aab-931a-94ff7ee7f3a8/brew-and-bloom-guide.md).*"}
{"step_index":169,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:02Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nUpdate the existing Brew & Bloom Café website. The website is already working, so do not rebuild it or change its existing design unnecessarily.\r\n\r\n## MAIN REQUIREMENT: WHATSAPP ORDERING\r\n\r\nReplace the current checkout submission flow with a direct WhatsApp ordering system.\r\n\r\nWhen a customer clicks \"Place Order\", \"Order on WhatsApp\", or the final checkout button, redirect them to WhatsApp with a pre-filled message containing their complete order.\r\n\r\n### 1. CONFIGURE THE RESTAURANT WHATSAPP NUMBER\r\n\r\nCreate a single configurable variable for the café owner's WhatsApp number.\r\n\r\nUse a placeholder such as:\r\n919876543210\r\n\r\nThis is an example only. Make it easy for the owner to replace it with their actual WhatsApp number, including the country code, without the + sign, spaces, or dashes.\r\n\r\nDo not invent or assume the real restaurant number.\r\n\r\n### 2. GENERATE THE ORDER MESSAGE AUTOMATICALLY\r\n\r\nRead the customer's actual cart and checkout information and construct a message like this:\r\n\r\nHello Brew & Bloom Café! I'd like to place an order.\r\n\r\nORDER DETAILS\r\nOrder ID: BB-123456\r\n\r\nItems:\r\n\r\n1. Cappuccino x 2 = ₹240\r\n2. Veg Sandwich x 1 = ₹120\r\n3. Chocolate Brownie x 1 = ₹100\r\n\r\nSubtotal: ₹460\r\nDelivery Fee: ₹30\r\nTotal Amount: ₹490\r\n\r\nORDER TYPE: Home Delivery\r\n\r\nCUSTOMER DETAILS\r\nName: Priyanshu\r\nPhone: 9876543210\r\nDelivery Address: [Customer's entered address]\r\nLandmark: [If provided]\r\nDelivery Instructions: [If provided]\r\n\r\nPAYMENT METHOD: Cash on Delivery\r\n\r\nPlease confirm my order and estimated delivery time. Thank you!\r\n\r\nGenerate the actual message dynamically from the customer's selected products, quantities, prices, delivery fee, order type, address and payment selection.\r\n\r\nDo not hardcode example products, customer details, or totals. Omit optional fields that the customer has not provided.\r\n\r\n### 3. WHATSAPP REDIRECTION\r\n\r\nWhen the customer clicks the final checkout button:\r\n\r\n1. Validate all required checkout fields.\r\n2. Validate that the cart contains at least one item.\r\n3.\n<truncated 897 bytes>\nign, colours and animations.\r\n* Display a loading state while preparing the WhatsApp message.\r\n* Prevent accidental repeated clicks.\r\n* Keep the customer on the checkout page if required fields are missing.\r\n* Show a clear error if the restaurant WhatsApp number has not been configured.\r\n\r\n### 5. ORDER STATUS AND HONEST CONFIRMATION\r\n\r\nOpening WhatsApp does not mean the order has been placed successfully.\r\n\r\nDo not show \"Order Confirmed\" or \"Payment Successful\" merely because the customer clicked the button or WhatsApp opened.\r\n\r\nExplain that the order is submitted only after the customer sends the message and the restaurant acknowledges it.\r\n\r\nDo not automatically mark an order as accepted, preparing, or out for delivery without a real backend confirmation.\r\n\r\n### 6. ORDER TYPE SUPPORT\r\n\r\nFor home delivery:\r\nInclude the complete delivery address, customer phone number, delivery instructions, and delivery fee.\r\n\r\nFor takeaway:\r\nInclude the selected pickup option and any pickup instructions. Do not require a delivery address.\r\n\r\nFor dine-in, if the existing website supports it:\r\nInclude the selected table or seating information if available.\r\n\r\n### 7. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS\r\n\r\n* Inspect the existing checkout implementation before making changes.\r\n* Reuse the existing cart and checkout state.\r\n* Do not break the current menu, quantity controls, price calculations, or responsive layout.\r\n* Do not add a QR code, payment gateway, or unnecessary backend.\r\n* Do not expose API keys or secrets.\r\n* Ensure the WhatsApp message is readable and correctly formatted on mobile.\r\n* Test the workflow with multiple products, different quantities, missing fields, delivery and takeaway orders, and special characters in the address.\r\n* Test that the configured WhatsApp number and all order details are correct.\r\n\r\nImplement the changes in the existing project, run the website, fix any errors, and report which tests passed.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-01T03:28:02+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":170,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:03Z","thinking":"The primary task is to integrate WhatsApp ordering into the existing website. The instructions explicitly state avoiding a full redesign. Focus will be on replacing the current checkout process with a WhatsApp redirect when the user clicks on specific buttons.\n\n\nA configurable variable for the restaurant's WhatsApp number is needed, using a placeholder to guide the user without assuming the actual number. The order message must be dynamically generated, pulling data from the customer's cart, checkout details (order ID, items, subtotals, delivery, customer details, and payment method). Validation of required fields must occur before redirecting to WhatsApp.\n\n\nFirst, the cart must be validated to ensure it contains items and the order total must be calculated accurately. Then a unique order reference will be generated. The WhatsApp message will be built dynamically and encoded for safe use in the URL, along with the restaurant's configured number. Finally, the WhatsApp conversation will be opened using the constructed URL.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lenovo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\brew-and-bloom\\\\js\\\\config.js\"","toolAction":"\"Inspecting config.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Read config.js\""}}]}
{"step_index":171,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-01T03:28:07+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-01T03:28:08+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/Lenovo/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/brew-and-bloom/js/config.js`\nTotal Lines: 111\nTotal Bytes: 5530\nShowing lines 1 to 111\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /**\n2:  * ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3:  * ║  BREW & BLOOM CAFÉ — CENTRAL CONFIGURATION              ║\n4:  * ║  Edit this file to customise your café platform.        ║\n5:  * ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n6:  */\n7: \n8: const CONFIG = {\n9: \n10:   /* ── CAFÉ IDENTITY ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n11:   cafe: {\n12:     name:        'Brew & Bloom Café',\n13:     tagline:     'Good Coffee. Slow Moments. Beautiful Days.',\n14:     address:     '[Sample Address], Near [Landmark], Haldia, West Bengal – 721657',\n15:     city:        'Haldia, West Bengal',\n16:     phone:       '+91 00000 00000',       // ← Replace with real number\n17:     email:       'hello@brewandbloom.in', // ← Replace with real email\n18:     whatsapp:    '910000000000',          // ← Replace (country code + number, no symbols)\n19:     instagram:   '#',                     // ← Replace with Instagram URL\n20:     facebook:    '#',                     // ← Replace with Facebook URL\n21:   },\n22: \n23:   /* ── RESTAURANT LOCATION ───────────────────────────────── */\n24:   // ⚠️ IMPORTANT: Replace with you\n<truncated 2437 bytes>\n───────────────────────── */\n69:   payment: {\n70:     codEnabled:     true,\n71:     upiEnabled:     true,\n72:     upiId:          'yourname@upi',  // ← Replace with your UPI ID\n73:     upiName:        'Brew & Bloom Café',\n74:     // Online gateway (Razorpay / Cashfree): set keyId below.\n75:     // Leave empty to show demo-mode UPI only.\n76:     razorpayKeyId:  '',              // ← Optional: Razorpay key_id\n77:   },\n78: \n79:   /* ── ORDER TRACKING ─────────────────────────────────────── */\n80:   tracking: {\n81:     // If Supabase is not configured, demo mode kicks in automatically.\n82:     // Demo simulates a driver moving from restaurant to customer.\n83:     locationUpdateIntervalMs: 5000,  // How often driver app sends GPS (ms)\n84:     demoRouteSteps: 20,              // Steps in simulated demo route\n85:   },\n86: \n87:   /* ── MAP ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n88:   map: {\n89:     defaultZoom: 14,\n90:     // OSRM public routing API (free, no key needed)\n91:     osrmBase: 'https://router.project-osrm.org/route/v1/driving',\n92:     // Tile server (OpenStreetMap — free, no key)\n93:     tileUrl: 'https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',\n94:     tileAttribution: '© <a href=\"https://www.openstreetmap.org/\">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors',\n95:   },\n96: \n97: };\n98: \n99: // Freeze so nothing accidentally mutates config\n100: Object.freeze(CONFIG);\n101: Object.freeze(CONFIG.cafe);\n102: Object.freeze(CONFIG.restaurant);\n103: Object.freeze(CONFIG.delivery);\n104: Object.freeze(CONFIG.tax);\n105: Object.freeze(CONFIG.supabase);\n106: Object.freeze(CONFIG.payment);\n107: Object.freeze(CONFIG.tracking);\n108: Object.freeze(CONFIG.map);\n109: \n110: export default CONFIG;\n111: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:08Z","thinking":"Found a likely configuration variable for the WhatsApp number within the project's configuration file. The prompt requires this number to be easily modified by the owner, so it needs to be clearly labeled as such and set to a placeholder value, not a real number. Will ensure the example includes the country code and avoid any formatting characters like spaces or dashes.\n\n\nThe configuration file will include a clearly labeled, editable variable for the restaurant's WhatsApp number, along with validation checks in the main script to handle missing or invalid configurations, prompting a clear error message. The second requirement focuses on automatically constructing order messages that will leverage the customer's cart and checkout data to provide a well-formatted output with order details, subtotal, total, and customer information.\n\n\nConstructing the order confirmation message requires dynamically assembling information from the order snapshot. The output format must include a unique order ID, an itemized list with quantities and prices, subtotal, and delivery fee. Conditional rendering for `Home Delivery`, `Takeaway`, or `Dine-In` order types is essential.\n\nWill incorporate GST calculation (or total amount) if applicable. Customer details (name, phone, delivery address, landmark, and delivery instructions) will be included based on availability.\n\n\nRequirement three necessitates implementing a client-side WhatsApp redirection. This involves field validation, cart item check, accurate total calculation, order reference generation, dynamic message building, and URL encoding. The redirection method will leverage the `wa.me` URL format to seamlessly open the WhatsApp conversation. Requirement four emphasizes validating the order summary structure, including order type-specific details such as delivery/pickup instructions or table information, and confirming a payment method.\n\n\nImplementing changes to the main checkout button to \"Place Order on WhatsApp\" with an icon and clear explanatory text is necessary to align with the prompt. Incorporating a loading state during message preparation and preventing accidental clicks is essential for a smooth user experience.\n\nThe system will maintain user state if required fields are missing and display an error if the restaurant's WhatsApp number is not set. Building the user experience modal to clarify that the order submission occurs *after* the WhatsApp message is sent to the restaurant is critical to being honest with the customer.\n\n\nRemoved the dynamic QR code implementation based on the explicit instruction. The focus shifts towards directly integrating the WhatsApp order submission. The existing checkout flow will be replaced by the WhatsApp redirection. The UI will include a \"Place Order on WhatsApp\" button with appropriate messaging. The generated WhatsApp message needs the order reference ID.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lenovo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\brew-and-bloom\\\\index.html\"","EndLine":"715","StartLine":"570","toolAction":"\"Reading checkout section in index.html\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect checkout modal HTML\""}}]}
