{"step_index":182,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:58:38Z","thinking":"Currently, the \"Place Order\" button triggers an order placement function, displays a success message, and redirects to an order tracking page. The new requirement necessitates redirecting users to WhatsApp instead. This code block needs to be replaced or modified to create a WhatsApp intent link.\n\n\nThe current order placement functionality needs to be replaced with a WhatsApp integration, including generating a pre-filled message with order details. Several UI changes are required, such as modifying the button text, adding a WhatsApp icon, and including an explanation for the user.  The loading state during message preparation and prevention of accidental clicks are also key. The misleading order confirmation messages must be removed, and order status updates must only happen upon real backend confirmation from the restaurant.\n\n\nFirst, the WhatsApp number configuration and validation logic needs to be integrated. An order reference ID must then be created. Finally, I will dynamically generate the WhatsApp message, incorporating order details, customer information, and payment method. The goal is to format a pre-filled WhatsApp message for the user to send.\n\n\nAnalyzing order types to determine the necessary customer details and payment information for the WhatsApp message. Considering differences between self-pickup, dine-in, and home delivery to format data appropriately. Updating the checkout modal in `index.html` to include a landmark field for home delivery orders, expanding available data.\n\n\nNow integrating the specified UI elements, including button text and helper text explaining the WhatsApp order process. A disclaimer will be added to clarify that opening WhatsApp doesn't confirm the order. A new status modal will be displayed after the WhatsApp link is opened, replacing the misleading \"Order Confirmed\" messages. This will feature the order ID and instruct the user to send the WhatsApp message for confirmation.\n\nNext, I need to test all required field validations and different order scenarios, ensuring the correct data is included in the WhatsApp message. Validating the WhatsApp number format and handling of special characters within address data will be important. After functionality is confirmed, I'll review `style.css` for visual consistency and adjust styles as needed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"/**\\n * ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\\n * ║  BREW & BLOOM CAFÉ — CENTRAL CONFIGURATION              ║\\n * ║  Edit this file to customise your café platform.        ║\\n * ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\\n */\\n\\n/**\\n * ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n * 📱 RESTAURANT WHATSAPP CONFIGURATION (SINGLE EDITABLE VARIABLE)\\n * ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n * Enter the café owner's WhatsApp number below.\\n * Format: Country code + Mobile number (digits only, no '+', spaces, or dashes).\\n * Example for India: '919876543210'\\n * ⚠️ Replace this placeholder with the café's actual WhatsApp number.\\n */\\nexport const RESTAURANT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER = '919876543210'; // ← EDIT THIS VARIABLE\\n\\nconst CONFIG = {\\n\\n  /* ── CAFÉ IDENTITY ─────────────────────────────────────── */\\n  cafe: {\\n    name:        'Brew & Bloom Café',\\n    tagline:     'Good Coffee. Slow Moments. Beautiful Days.',\\n    address:     '[Sample Address], Near City Center, Haldia, West Bengal – 721657',\\n    city:        'Haldia, West Bengal',\\n    phone:       '+91 98765 43210',\\n    email:       'hello@brewandbloom.in',\\n    whatsapp:    RESTAURANT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER, // Links to the single variable above\\n    instagram:   '#',\\n    facebook:    '#',\\n  },\\n\\n  /* ── RESTAURANT LOCATION ─────────────────\n<truncated 2396 bytes>","Description":"\"Add single configurable RESTAURANT_WHATSAPP_NUMBER constant at top of config.js as requested.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Lenovo\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\brew-and-bloom\\\\js\\\\config.js\"","toolAction":"\"Updating config.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Configure restaurant WhatsApp variable\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
